\subsection{Unified prompting and attention masks}
Inputs and attention are formatted per task (\cref{fig:prompt}).
\textbf{MMU:} the input is \{[MMU], image tokens $u$, language tokens $l$\}. Image tokens precede text so they can attend to each other, and the LLM predicts next language tokens, $\hat{H}^{L}=\pi_\theta^{\mathrm{MMU}}(I,L)$.
\textbf{PRE:} the input is \{[PRE], language tokens $l$, current image tokens $v_t$\}. Image tokens follow the text so they attend to all prior tokens, and future image tokens are predicted at aligned positions rather than as next-token prediction over the sequence, $\hat{H}^{O_{t+\Delta t}}=\pi_\theta^{\mathrm{PRE}}(O_t,L)$.

