\subsection{Joint prediction and understanding for action}
Given $(O_t,L)$, UP-VLA first generates a scene description $s=\pi_\theta^{\mathrm{MMU}}(O_t,L_{\mathrm{prompt}})$ with a prompt such as ``describe this image'', and embeds additional visual information $E_1(O'_t)$ into language space. The extended instruction is $L'=[E_1(O'_t),s,L]$. The model then jointly predicts future image tokens and actions, $(\hat{H}^{O_{t+\Delta t}},\hat{H}^{A_{t:t+\Delta t}})=\pi_\theta^{\mathrm{PRE}}(O_t,L')$, so actions attend to both semantic (MMU) tokens and predictive visual tokens. A lightweight policy head (a single-layer attention pooling MAP followed by an MLP) maps action tokens to continuous actions, $\hat{a}_{t:t+\Delta t}=\mathrm{MLP}(\mathrm{MAP}(\hat{H}^{A_{t:t+\Delta t}}))$.

\subsection{Training objectives and pipeline}
The MMU loss is cross-entropy over next text tokens, $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{MMU}}=\sum_i\log p_\theta(l_i\mid u,l_{1:i-1})$. The prediction loss is cross-entropy over future image tokens, $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{PRE}}=\sum_j\log p_\theta(v'_j\mid l,v_{1:M})$, modeling $P(O_{t+\Delta t}\mid O_t,L)=\prod_{j=1}^{M}p_\theta(v'_j\mid l,v_{1:M})$. The action loss is $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ACT}}=\|\hat{a}_{\mathrm{pos}}-a_{\mathrm{pos}}\|_2^2+\mathrm{BCE}(\hat{a}_{\mathrm{end}},a_{\mathrm{end}})$. The total loss is
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}=\lambda_1\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{MMU}}+\lambda_2\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{PRE}}+\lambda_3\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ACT}}.
\end{equation}
Training has two stages. In stage 1 we pre-train on a mix of MMU data (LLaVA-tuning-665k, \citealp{liu2024visual}) and PRE data (Bridge, 25k demonstrations, \citealp{walke2023bridgedata}) with task-specific prompts and masks. In stage 2 we fine-tune actions on downstream robot data with joint prediction-and-understanding prompting, continuing MMU co-training to retain semantic capabilities.

\textbf{Test time.} Given $O_t$ and $L$, the model generates a scene description $s$ via MMU, embeds $E_1(O'_t)$, forms $L'$, runs the PRE pathway to obtain future tokens and action tokens, decodes actions via MAP+MLP for execution, and repeats.

\section{Experiments}
\subsection{Setup}
\textbf{Simulation.} We evaluate on CALVIN ABC$\rightarrow$D and ABCD$\rightarrow$D, with four scenes A/B/C/D, reporting the average length of tasks completed in a row.
\textbf{Real world.} We use a Franka Emika Panda arm with more than 2k demonstrations over 6 skills, and evaluate seen tasks, unseen-object grasping, and precise operations (e.g., cable routing, small-object grasping), with 20 trials per task (\cref{fig:env}).
\textbf{Baselines.} VLA-based: RoboFlamingo \citep{li2023vision}, 3D-VLA \citep{zhen20243d}, UP-VLA-RT-2 (an RT-2-style variant) and RT-1 \citep{brohan2022rt}. Prediction-based: GR-1 \citep{wu2023unleashing}, SuSIE \citep{black2023zero}, UniPi \citep{du2024learning}, 3D Diffuser Actor \citep{ke20243d} and Diffusion Policy \citep{chi2023diffusionpolicy}. We also ablate UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu, a GR-1-like model with the same backbone.

