\subsection{Simulation results}
On CALVIN ABC$\rightarrow$D (\cref{table1}), UP-VLA reaches an average length of 4.08, versus 3.06 for GR-1, 3.35 for 3D Diffuser Actor, 2.47 for RoboFlamingo and 1.44 for UP-VLA-RT-2; this is a 33\% improvement over GR-1. Its chain success rates are 0.928, 0.865, 0.815, 0.769 and 0.699 for one to five tasks. On ABCD$\rightarrow$D (\cref{table2}), UP-VLA reaches 4.42 against 4.21 for GR-1 and 4.09 for RoboFlamingo. The larger margin in the zero-shot ABC$\rightarrow$D setting is consistent with its improved generalization to the unseen scene D.

