\subsection{Ablations}
\Cref{table:ablate} ablates components, reporting CALVIN ABC$\rightarrow$D average length and real-world seen/unseen success. Removing prediction is most damaging on CALVIN (4.08 to 1.44), showing prediction is crucial for spatial and dynamics grounding. Removing Bridge pre-training lowers CALVIN to 2.74 and real-world unseen to 0.30, so predictive pre-training helps downstream performance. Removing MMU leaves CALVIN (3.89) and seen tasks (0.85) near the full model but drops unseen-object success from 0.58 to 0.20, and removing MMU conditioning gives 3.99 / 0.80 / 0.50: MMU is critical for semantic generalization, and conditioning actions on MMU scene descriptions further helps.

